.TH CLAVIRIO 1 2026-11-11 "clavirio 0.4.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clavirio \- terminal typing tutor with a virtual keyboard, lessons and session history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clavirio
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-w
.RI [ n ]]
.RB [ \-t
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR list ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B clavirio
.BR \-h | \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clavirio
teaches touch typing in the terminal.
It shows your speed and accuracy as you type, highlights the next key and the
finger to use on a virtual keyboard, and saves your session history.
.PP
Lessons teach the keyboard row by row, for the QWERTY, Dvorak and Colemak
layouts.
Each row follows the same seven steps: index pair, middle pair, ring pair,
pinky pair, reach pair, full row, and the row with Shift.
Lessons 1 to 21 follow the chosen layout; lessons 22 to 27 cover numbers and
symbols and are the same for every layout.
.PP
Practice modes offer random words from the English 200 or 1k lists, code terms
for several programming languages, timed sessions, your weak keys, common
bigrams, quotes, and Zen mode for free typing.
.PP
Without options,
.B clavirio
opens the interactive menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-file " file
Load
.I file
as the typing text.
Curly quotes, dashes and ellipses become characters you can type
.RB ( \(aq ,
.BR \(dq ,
.BR \- ,
.BR \-\- ,
.BR ... ),
separately stored accents are joined to their letters, tabs become four spaces,
and invisible characters such as soft hyphens are removed.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-words " [\fIn\fP]"
Practice with
.I n
random words, from 1 to 10000 (default: 100).
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds" "\fR, \fP\-\-time " seconds
Practice for the given number of seconds, from 1 to 3600.
.TP
.BI \-l " list" "\fR, \fP\-\-list " list
The word or code list for
.B \-w
and
.BR \-t :
.BR 200 " (default), " 1k ,
.BR rust ,
.BR python ,
.BR javascript " (or " js ),
.BR go ,
.BR c " (or " cpp ", " c++ ),
.BR java ,
or
.BR html " (or " css ).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-punctuation
Add punctuation to word or code practice, for this run only.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-numbers
Add numbers to word or code practice, for this run only.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Only one of
.BR \-t ,
.B \-w
and
.B \-f
is used:
.B \-t
wins over
.BR \-w ,
and
.B \-w
over
.BR \-f .
.SH KEYS
.SS Main menu
.TP
.BR Up / Down " or " k / j
Move through the menu.
.TP
.B Enter
Start the selected lesson or practice.
.TP
.B m
Switch between lessons and practice.
.TP
.B h
Show the session history.
.TP
.B t
Switch the theme (dark or light).
.TP
.B l
Switch the layout (QWERTY, Dvorak or Colemak).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-F
Load a file.
.TP
.B 1
Show or hide which finger to use.
This works only while the key hints are shown.
.TP
.B 2
Show or hide the key hints.
.TP
.B 3
Show or hide the keyboard.
This works only when the terminal is large enough to fit it.
.TP
.B 4
Turn error stop on or off.
With error stop on, a mistake must be corrected with Backspace before typing
continues.
.TP
.BR 5 ", " 6
Turn punctuation or numbers on or off (practice only).
.TP
.B 7
Turn shift error on or off: a capital or symbol typed with the Shift key on its
own hand counts as a mistake.
This needs a terminal with the kitty keyboard protocol, such as kitty, Ghostty
or foot.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit.
.SS Typing
.TP
.B Backspace
Correct a mistake.
.TP
.B Esc
Open the pause menu (in Zen mode, stop).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-R
Restart (not in Zen mode).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-F
Load a file.
.SS Finished screen
.TP
.B r
Restart.
.TP
.B w
Practice the weak keys of the session, or your saved weak keys if the session
had none.
.TP
.B n
Next lesson (lessons only).
.TP
.B Esc
Back to the menu.
.SS Pause menu
.TP
.BR Up / Down " or " k / j
Move through the menu.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
Go to the first or last item.
.TP
.BR Space ", " Enter
Choose the selected item.
.TP
.B r
Restart.
.TP
.B n
Next lesson (lessons only).
.TP
.B Esc
Back to the menu.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SS History
.TP
.BR Up / Down " or " k / j
Scroll.
.TP
.B Esc
Back to the menu.
.SS Anywhere
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.TP
.B Esc
Close an error message.
In the pause menu and the history, Esc goes back to the menu instead.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.clavirio/settings.toml
Layout, theme and display settings, saved as they change.
.TP
.I ~/.clavirio/history.json
Past sessions with their speed, accuracy and duration.
.TP
.I ~/.clavirio/keystats.json
Hits and misses for each key, used for weak key practice.
.PP
A file that can't be parsed is kept next to it as a timestamped
.I .bak
file before it is rewritten.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
The folder that holds
.IR .clavirio .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B clavirio \-w 50 \-l 1k
50 random words from the English 1k list.
.TP
.B clavirio \-t 30 \-l python
A 30-second session with Python terms.
.TP
.B clavirio \-w \-p \-n
100 random words with punctuation and numbers.
.TP
.B clavirio \-f notes.txt
Type the text of
.IR notes.txt .
.SH AUTHOR
Alexander Alexandrov and contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://clavir.io
.UE
